# Nemotron 3 Super 120B-A12B on eight nodes of 8 GPUs, as Megatron-Bridge's performance
# summary benchmarks it (26.06 on 64 B300s, EP=8, a global batch of 512 rows of 8192 in
# microbatches of a row a GPU: 7,867 tokens a second a GPU in MXFP8, 8,131 in NVFP4).
# The experts are split over a node's GPUs and their shards over the nodes, sent there
# by NCCL EP and routed by random logits, as Megatron's are. The MTP module stays in
# bfloat16. In NVFP4, attention, the latent projections and the last 14 layers do too,
# and Mamba's output projection is in MXFP8 (Megatron's te_quant.cfg).
#
#   python scripts/benchmark.py run examples/benchmarks/megatron_super.bux --out new.json   # on each host
use nemotron_3_super_120b_a12b

experts.random_logits = true

mesh    = mesh(fsdp=8, expert=8)
methods = methods(moe=nccl_ep, capacity=1.25, microbatches=8)

data      = synthetic
optimizer = adamw(lr=3e-4)
seq_len   = 8192
batch     = 512
steps     = 12
log       = log(every=3)
precision = mxfp8: precision(compute=bfloat16, matmuls=mxfp8, roles=roles(mtp=compute))
          | nvfp4: precision(compute=bfloat16, matmuls=nvfp4, last=14,
                             roles=roles(q=compute, kv=compute, o=compute, latent=compute,
                                         recurrence_out=mxfp8, mtp=compute))
